From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Lippautz <mlippautz@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:38:02 -0700
Subject: gin: Use v8::CppHeapExternal for CallbackHolderBase

Migrate gin::internal::CallbackHolderBase from gin::Wrappable to
cppgc::GarbageCollected<CallbackHolderBase> wrapped in
v8::CppHeapExternal. Because v8::CppHeapExternal is a primitive
HeapObject (subtype of v8::Data) rather than a v8::Object, it has no
creation v8::Context and does not retain a NativeContext when cached on
a v8::FunctionTemplate or v8::ObjectTemplate.

This also allows moving the ObjectTemplate cache back from
gin::PerContextData to gin::PerIsolateData.

Backported so Electron's gin_helper callback holders can use the cppgc
based CallbackHolderBase before the Chromium roll that contains this CL.
This patch should be removed once Chromium includes crrev.com/c/8485746
(first released in 157.0.8091.0).

Bug: 567169217, 568151990
Change-Id: If006b7738204b7cbda53698aa6c74fcdaea8950a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8485746
Reviewed-by: Andreas Haas <ahaas@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Michael Lippautz <mlippautz@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1711265}

